      draw: 'All cards are dealt at hand start; no draw step exists.',
      discard: 'Cards leave hand only by being played to tricks.',
      pass: 'Players cannot pass; they must play one card each trick.',
      bid: 'No bidding system is used in this ruleset.',
      meld: 'Game to Lose does not include meld declarations.',
      go_out: 'Hands end after 13 tricks, not via a go-out action.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 13 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Avoid winning tricks that contain point-bearing cards. The first player to reach 121 points loses the match.',
      'Turn-flow example: The pitcher leads to the first trick; the suit led becomes trump for the hand. Players must follow suit if able, otherwise may play any card. Highest card of led suit wins unless trump is played, then highest trump wins. Trick winner leads next trick. Points are pegged during play for certain trump cards and all fives; after all 13 tricks, card points are counted and the player with highest total pegs the Eight bonus.',
      'Scoring example: Immediate pegging during trick play: trump A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1, 9=9, 5=10, and non-trump 5s=5 each. After 13 tricks, count A/K/Q/J/10 in won cards; highest count pegs 8 (or 4 each in a two-way tie). First player whose total reaches 121 or more loses..',
